  },
  data: {
    LLM: '1. **Lead**: Non-dealer leads first trick. 2. **Follow suit**: Second player must follow suit if possible from hand or currently face-up table cards. 3. **If void**: Any available card may be played; trumps can cut. 4. **Trick winner**: Higher card of same suit wins, otherwise trump wins, otherwise first played card wins when neither card is trump. 5. **Card availability**: You may play from hand or any face-up table card; when a face-up table card is played, its face-down undercard is revealed for future tricks. 6. **Continuation**: Winner of each trick leads next. 7. **End**: After 15 tricks, compare trick totals against quota thresholds.',
    Player: '1. **Lead**: Non-dealer leads first trick. 2. **Follow suit**: Second player must follow suit if possible from hand or currently face-up table cards. 3. **If void**: Any available card may be played; trumps can cut. 4. **Trick winner**: Higher card of same suit wins, otherwise trump wins, otherwise first played card wins when neither card is trump. 5. **Card availability**: You may play from hand or any face-up table card; when a face-up table card is played, its face-down undercard is revealed for future tricks. 6. **Continuation**: Winner of each trick leads next. 7. **End**: After 15 tricks, compare trick totals against quota thresholds.',
    objective: 'Win enough tricks relative to your role quota: dealer targets more than 7, non-dealer targets more than 8, and 7-8 exact is a tie.',
    gameplay: '1. **Lead**: Non-dealer leads first trick. 2. **Follow suit**: Second player must follow suit if possible from hand or currently face-up table cards. 3. **If void**: Any available card may be played; trumps can cut. 4. **Trick winner**: Higher card of same suit wins, otherwise trump wins, otherwise first played card wins when neither card is trump. 5. **Card availability**: You may play from hand or any face-up table card; when a face-up table card is played, its face-down undercard is revealed for future tricks. 6. **Continuation**: Winner of each trick leads next. 7. **End**: After 15 tricks, compare trick totals against quota thresholds.',
    keyRules: [
      '7 of hearts and 7 of spades are always top trumps when special-sevens rule is used.',
      'Those two sevens count as trumps, not as hearts/spades for follow-suit in non-trump suits.',
      'Second hand must follow suit if able; otherwise may discard or trump.',
      'Exact 7 tricks for dealer and 8 for non-dealer is a draw.',
      'Non-dealer always chooses trump after the initial 5-card deal.',
    ],
